IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-art11-application`
IMPORT `g4-art11-decision`
IMPORT `g4-tests-fixtures`

-- g4-tests-art11-decision.l4: tests for Article 11(4) to (7) and (9), whose expected values were decided from the Law's text BEFORE the encoding was run.
-- Every case is the base case (the applicant complies, the six matters are found, no bar applies) with the named facts changed, and is named for those facts.
-- The default reading is used throughout; the other readings of F4.3 and F4.4 are in g4-tests-forks.l4.

§ `Tests of Article 11(4) to (7) and (9)`

§§ `Article 11(4) -- the duty to register, and each of the six matters failing alone`

-- The base case: a Jersey company, complying, with the six matters found and no bar.
#ASSERT `the applicant complies in` `the base case`
#ASSERT `the six matters are found in` `the base case`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the base case` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the decision in` `the base case` EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`)

-- (a) "the applicant meets the charity test, or will do so on registration".
`the case where the charity test is not met and will not be met` MEANS `the base case` `but with the charity test as` FALSE
`the case where the charity test is not met now but will be met on registration` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the charity test as` FALSE) `but with the findings as` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on meeting the charity test on registration as` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the six matters are found in` `the case where the charity test is not met and will not be met`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the charity test is not met and will not be met` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the six matters are found in` `the case where the charity test is not met now but will be met on registration`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the charity test is not met now but will be met on registration` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`

-- (b) "the constitution of the applicant is a written document".
`the case where the constitution is not a written document` MEANS `the base case` `but with the findings as` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a written constitution as` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(b) the constitution of the applicant is a written document` `the base findings`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(b) the constitution of the applicant is a written document` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a written constitution as` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the constitution is not a written document` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

-- (c) "the applicant (i) is a Jersey entity, or (ii) carries out, or intends to carry out, in or from within Jersey, an activity that is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial".
`the case of a foreign entity with no activity in Jersey` MEANS `the base case` `but with the applicant as` `a foreign entity that has applied`
`the case of a foreign entity with a substantial activity in Jersey` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the applicant as` `a foreign entity that has applied`) `but with the findings as` `the findings for a foreign entity with a substantial activity in Jersey`
`the case of a foreign entity with an activity in Jersey that is not substantial` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the applicant as` `a foreign entity that has applied`) `but with the findings as` ((`the base findings` `but with the finding on an activity in or from within Jersey as` TRUE) `but with the opinion on a substantial activity as` FALSE)
`the case of a foreign entity with no activity in Jersey but the opinion that it is substantial` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the applicant as` `a foreign entity that has applied`) `but with the findings as` (`the base findings` `but with the opinion on a substantial activity as` TRUE)
`the case of a Jersey NPO body corporate with no activity in Jersey` MEANS `the base case` `but with the applicant as` `a Jersey NPO body corporate that has applied`
`the case of a Jersey company with an activity in Jersey that is not substantial` MEANS `the base case` `but with the findings as` ((`the base findings` `but with the finding on an activity in or from within Jersey as` TRUE) `but with the opinion on a substantial activity as` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(c)(i) the applicant is a Jersey entity` `a Jersey company that has applied`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(c)(i) the applicant is a Jersey entity` `a foreign entity that has applied`
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(c)(ii) the applicant carries out an activity that is substantial` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(c)(ii) the applicant carries out an activity that is substantial` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(c)(ii) the applicant carries out an activity that is substantial` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(c)(ii) the applicant carries out an activity that is substantial` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` `a Jersey company that has applied` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` `a Jersey NPO body corporate that has applied` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` `a foreign entity that has applied` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` `a foreign entity that has applied` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` `a foreign entity that has applied` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` `a foreign entity that has applied` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case of a foreign entity with no activity in Jersey` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case of a foreign entity with a substantial activity in Jersey` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case of a foreign entity with an activity in Jersey that is not substantial` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case of a foreign entity with no activity in Jersey but the opinion that it is substantial` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case of a Jersey NPO body corporate with no activity in Jersey` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case of a Jersey company with an activity in Jersey that is not substantial` EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`

-- (d) "the applicant has a principal address in Jersey, within the meaning of Article 8(4)".
`the case where the applicant has no principal address in Jersey` MEANS `the base case` `but with the principal address as` FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(d) the requirement is met` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(d) the requirement is met` FALSE
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the applicant has no principal address in Jersey` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
-- A foreign entity with a substantial activity still needs a principal address in Jersey.
`the case of a foreign entity with a substantial activity in Jersey and no principal address in Jersey` MEANS `the case of a foreign entity with a substantial activity in Jersey` `but with the principal address as` FALSE
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case of a foreign entity with a substantial activity in Jersey and no principal address in Jersey` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

-- (e) "the name of the applicant is not undesirable under Article 12".
`the case where the name is undesirable` MEANS `the base case` `but with the name as` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(e) the name of the applicant is not undesirable under Article 12` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(e) the name of the applicant is not undesirable under Article 12` TRUE
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the name is undesirable` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

-- (f) "no other ground for refusal, prescribed under paragraph (7), applies or should be applied".
`the case where a prescribed ground of mandatory refusal applies` MEANS `the base case` `but with the findings as` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a mandatory prescribed ground as` TRUE)
`the case where a prescribed ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` MEANS `the base case` `but with the findings as` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground as` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `the default reading` `the base findings`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `the default reading` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a mandatory prescribed ground as` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4)(f) no other ground for refusal prescribed under Article 11(7) applies or should be applied` `the default reading` (`the base findings` `but with the finding on a discretionary prescribed ground as` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a prescribed ground of mandatory refusal applies` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a prescribed ground of discretionary refusal should be applied` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

-- The duty and the refusal as regulative rules, run against what the Commissioner does.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `the duty to register in` `the base case` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to register in` `the base case` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `the Commissioner registers the applicant` AT 20

-- With the six matters found there is no duty to refuse.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to refuse in` `the base case` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- Where a matter fails, the duty to register does not arise and the duty to refuse does.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to register in` `the case where the name is undesirable` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `the duty to refuse in` `the case where the name is undesirable` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to refuse in` `the case where the name is undesirable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `the Commissioner refuses to register the applicant` AT 20

§§ `Article 11(4) chapeau, 11(5) -- an application that does not comply (trap T10, fork F4.3)`

-- "If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5)": each of the three conditions failing alone, with the six matters otherwise found.
`the case where the copy of the constitution is missing` MEANS `the base case` `but with the application as` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)
`the case where the application does not state that it holds the governors' declarations` MEANS `the base case` `but with Article 19(5) complied with as` FALSE
`the case where the procedure under the Regulations was not followed` MEANS `the base case` `but with the application as` (`the base application with other requirements` `other requirements: the procedure under the Regulations was not followed`)
`the case where the copy of the constitution is missing and the name is undesirable` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the application as` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)) `but with the name as` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the applicant complies in` `the case where the copy of the constitution is missing`
#ASSERT NOT `the applicant complies in` `the case where the application does not state that it holds the governors' declarations`
#ASSERT NOT `the applicant complies in` `the case where the procedure under the Regulations was not followed`
#ASSERT `the six matters are found in` `the case where the copy of the constitution is missing`
-- Discriminating case of F4.3 (trap T10, case B): the six matters are found but the copy of the constitution is missing. On the default reading neither duty arises.
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the copy of the constitution is missing` EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the application does not state that it holds the governors' declarations` EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the procedure under the Regulations was not followed` EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the copy of the constitution is missing and the name is undesirable` EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
-- No duty means no decision to report.
#ASSERT `the decision in` `the case where the copy of the constitution is missing` EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to register in` `the case where the copy of the constitution is missing` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to refuse in` `the case where the copy of the constitution is missing` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

§§ `Article 11(4), 19(9)(c), 20(1)(c) -- the duty to register against the bars on granting (trap T10, fork F4.4)`

#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` EQUALS `the Commissioner must not yet grant the application`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` EQUALS `the Commissioner must not register the applicant`
-- A court order is not temporary, so it comes first when both bars apply.
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` EQUALS `the Commissioner must not register the applicant`
-- A bar on granting does not turn a refusal into anything else.
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the name is undesirable` EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT `the duty in` `the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the copy of the constitution is missing` EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
-- Neither bar is a decision under Article 11(4) or (5).
#ASSERT `the decision in` `the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the decision in` `the case where the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The duty to register does not arise while a bar applies.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to register in` `the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `the duty to register in` `the case where the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

§§ `The decision of the Commissioner as other provisions name it (IP27)`

#ASSERT `the decision in` `the case where the name is undesirable` EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner refuses`)
#ASSERT `the decision in` `the case where the charity test is not met and will not be met` EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner refuses`)
#ASSERT `the decision in` `the case where the charity test is not met now but will be met on registration` EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`)

§§ `Article 11(6) -- guidance on whether an activity is substantial`

-- (a)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(6)(a) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on whether an activity is substantial` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(6)(a) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on whether an activity is substantial` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `publish and maintain guidance on whether an activity is substantial`) AT 10

-- (b), Article 5(6) applied: the consultation and the report, each limb alone missing.
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the consultation and the report are as Article 5(6) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the consultation and the report are as Article 5(6) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the consultation and the report are as Article 5(6) requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the consultation and the report are as Article 5(6) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the consultation and the report are as Article 5(6) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(6)(b) before issuing or amending the guidance the Commissioner must consult and publish a report` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(6)(b) before issuing or amending the guidance the Commissioner must consult and publish a report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `consult, and publish a report on the consultation, before issuing or amending the guidance`) AT 5

-- (b), Article 5(7) applied: "Within a reasonable time after issuing or amending guidance": the default reading takes the caller's determination, whatever the dates.
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `the default reading` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the copy was provided to the Minister within a reasonable time` `the default reading` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 2) NOTHING

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(6)(b) the Commissioner must provide the Minister with a copy of the guidance and the report` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(6)(b) the Commissioner must provide the Minister with a copy of the guidance and the report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `provide the Minister with a copy of the guidance and the report`) AT 20

-- (b), Article 5(8) applied: "as soon as practicable after the Minister receives" them.
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable` `the default reading` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 9 1) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister laid the copy before the States as soon as practicable` `the default reading` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 2) NOTHING

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister must lay a copy of the guidance and the report before the States` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(6)(b) the Minister must lay a copy of the guidance and the report before the States` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `lay a copy of the guidance and the report before the States`) AT 30

-- The whole sequence for one issue of the guidance, from consultation to the States.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(6) the guidance from consultation to the States` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `consult, and publish a report on the consultation, before issuing or amending the guidance`) AT 5
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `publish and maintain guidance on whether an activity is substantial`) AT 10

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(6) the guidance from consultation to the States` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `consult, and publish a report on the consultation, before issuing or amending the guidance`) AT 5
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `publish and maintain guidance on whether an activity is substantial`) AT 10
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `provide the Minister with a copy of the guidance and the report`) AT 20
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `lay a copy of the guidance and the report before the States`) AT 30

-- (c)
